  "worked_solution": "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\u0394x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+i\u0394x$ with $\u0394x=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=4$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is \n\n$$\n\u0394x=\\frac{4-0}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\u0394x & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+i\u0394x)\u0394x \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4+i).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
